## 125-Valid palindrome

## Approach 1: Two Pointers — Optimal
# Idea
We need to check whether a string is a palindrome after:
Ignoring all non-alphanumeric characters.
Treating uppercase and lowercase letters as the same.

I use two pointers:
--  left starts from the beginning.
--  right starts from the end.
--  If left points to a non-alphanumeric character, move left forward.
--  If right points to a non-alphanumeric character, move right backward.
--  When both characters are valid, convert them to lowercase and compare them.
--  If they are different, return false.
--  Otherwise, move both pointers inward.
--  If the pointers finish without finding a mismatch, return true.

## Complexity
Time: O(n)
Space: O(1)

SOLUTION :
class Solution {
    public boolean isPalindrome(String s) {

        int left = 0;
        int right = s.length() - 1;

        while (left <= right) {

            if (Character.isLetterOrDigit(s.charAt(left)) &&
                Character.isLetterOrDigit(s.charAt(right))) {

                if (Character.toLowerCase(s.charAt(left)) !=
                    Character.toLowerCase(s.charAt(right))) {

                    return false;
                }

                left++;
                right--;

            } else if (!Character.isLetterOrDigit(s.charAt(left))) {

                left++;

            } else if (!Character.isLetterOrDigit(s.charAt(right))) {

                right--;
            }
        }

        return true;
    }
}

