## Approach 2: Regex + StringBuilder
# Idea
Instead of skipping non-alphanumeric characters using two pointers, we can first clean the entire string.

--  Remove all non-alphanumeric characters using replaceAll().
--  Convert the string to lowercase.
--  Reverse the cleaned string using StringBuilder.
--  Compare the original cleaned string with the reversed string.

For example:
"A man, a plan, a canal: Panama"
                ↓
"amanaplanacanalpanama"
                ↓ reverse
"amanaplanacanalpanama"
                ↓
true

## Complexity
Time: O(n)
Space: O(n)

SOLUTION :
class Solution {
    public boolean isPalindrome(String s) {

        // Remove all non-alphanumeric characters
        s = s.replaceAll("[^a-zA-Z0-9]", "");

        // Convert to lowercase
        s = s.toLowerCase();

        // Reverse the string
        String rev = new StringBuilder(s).reverse().toString();

        // Compare original and reversed strings
        return s.equals(rev);
    }
}
